I'm a little afraid of this.

Before - we use `array-push` by default, if no `browserslist` or `output.environment.dynamicImport: true`
Now - we use `module`, because by default `output.environment.dynamicImport` is `conditionallyOptimistic` when no `browserslist` or `output.environment.dynamicImport` is undefined:
```js
F(environment, "dynamicImport", () =>
		conditionallyOptimistic(
			/** @type {boolean | undefined} */ (tp && tp.dynamicImport),
			output.module
		)
	);
```

But because `outputModule` is in `experiments` I think it is good idea and better DX
